  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the total number of votes that each party received by rounding to the nearest hundred.\n\n- The Green Party: $1\\,020⟶1\\,000$\n\n- The Labour Party: $3\\,022⟶3\\,000$\n\nSo the total number of votes received was approximately $1\\,000+3\\,000=4\\,000.$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of Labour Party votes to total votes (expressed as a fraction) is approximately\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\,000}{4\\,000}.\n$$\n\nDividing the numerator and denominator by $1\\,000$ gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\,000÷1\\,000}{4\\,000÷1\\,000}=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ratio of Labour Party votes to total votes is approximately $\\frac{3}{4}.$",
